<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/music">Music</a> controls what plays through each kiosk's speakers. The row of kiosks along the top
        shows what every kiosk is playing right now. Select one, and everything else on the page applies to it.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Choosing a kiosk">
        <ul>
            <li>Each kiosk shows a dot: green while it's playing, orange when it's paused or stopped, and an empty
                circle when it's <strong>Offline</strong>.</li>
            <li>The page remembers the kiosk you chose on this device.</li>
            <li>An offline kiosk can't be controlled. It may still be playing music it saved earlier, and its
                controls come back by themselves as soon as it reconnects.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Now playing">
        <ul>
            <li>The player shows the song, its album, and the playlist it's playing from.</li>
            <li>The controls are <strong>Shuffle</strong>, <strong>Previous</strong>, play and pause,
                <strong>Next</strong>, and repeat (off, the playlist, or this song). Shuffle and repeat show a dot
                underneath while they're on.</li>
            <li><strong>Previous</strong> restarts the song if it's more than 3 seconds in; press it again to go back
                to the song before.</li>
            <li>Drag the timeline to jump to a point in the song. Select the time on the left to switch between time
                played and time left.</li>
            <li>Drag the volume slider, or select the speaker to mute and unmute.</li>
            <li><strong>Up next</strong> lists the next few songs. If the music schedule is about to change playlist,
                it says so here.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            On a phone, a small player appears along the bottom once you scroll down to the songs, so you can pause
            or skip without scrolling back up. Select it to jump back to the full player.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Playing music">
        <ul>
            <li>Choose a playlist, or <strong>All songs</strong> for the whole library.</li>
            <li><strong>Play</strong> plays the playlist in order from the top. <strong>Shuffle</strong> plays every
                song once, in a random order, before any song repeats.</li>
            <li>Select a song to play it. In a playlist, the songs after it follow; in <strong>All songs</strong>,
                just that song plays.</li>
            <li>Use the search box to find a song by its name or album.</li>
            <li>Turning shuffle off carries on in playlist order from the song that's playing.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Managing playlists">
        <FluentText>
            Admins and people with the CanManagePlaylists role can change playlists. Upload songs in the
            <a href="/files">File Manager</a>: audio files are added to the library automatically.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>New playlist</strong> at the end of the playlist list creates one, with a name and an
                optional description.</li>
            <li>The pencil and bin beside a playlist's <strong>Play</strong> button rename and delete it. A
                playlist used by the music schedule or an automation rule can't be deleted until you choose another
                playlist there.</li>
            <li>A song's <strong>⋯</strong> menu adds it to another playlist, moves it up or down, or removes it from
                this playlist. Removing a song doesn't delete it from the library.</li>
            <li>On a computer you can also drag a song by its handle to reorder the playlist.</li>
            <li>Changes reach a kiosk that's playing the playlist straight away, without interrupting the song.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
